See, I played glHack a few times, and I noticed a wonderful feature.
Everytime a value in the status line changes (like, HP, EXP, Gold, AC,
...), its color becomes either green (if it was a good change) or red
(if it was a bad change). If there was no change it stays the default
color (usually gray).

Example: (Beginning of the game) I pick up a splint mail which I think
is better than my current armor. I press T to remove the old armor, AC
increases from 7 to 10, turns red. Then I press W and select the new
armor, AC decreases from 10 to 6, turns green.

Another example: Level-up: Max-HP, current HP, Str and Con increase and
turn green. At one glance I see which values have changed.


So I dare ask a question: Is it possible to enable this feature for the
ordinary (console) Nethack? I know about the hpmon patch, but this is
not what I'm looking for. Maybe there is a possibility of extracting
the changes from the glHack source and modifying the "real" Nethack
source accordingly?

